<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.IO.ManagedSqlite</RootNamespace>
    <TargetFrameworks>net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <AssemblyName>Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.IO.SQLite3</AssemblyName>
    <Platforms>AnyCPU;x64</Platforms>
    <Configurations>Debug;Release;Rsharp_app_release;mzkit;mzkit_win32;gcmodeller_desktop;nuget_release;MEMI-Desktop</Configurations>
    <AutoGenerateBindingRedirects>true</AutoGenerateBindingRedirects>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>True</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>GPL-3.0-or-later</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>http://scibasic.net/</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/xieguigang/sciBASIC</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <Version>1.0.9758.20045</Version>
    <AssemblyVersion>1.0.9758.20045</AssemblyVersion>
    <Title>Managed SQLite3 Database File Reader</Title>
    <Description>A pure managed parser and writer for SQLite3 database files that decodes the database header, B-tree pages, master table and column types, exposes tables and rows, and parses CREATE TABLE schema SQL without the native SQLite engine.</Description>
    <AssemblyTitle>Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.IO.SQLite3</AssemblyTitle>
    <Authors>xieguigang &lt;I@xieguigang.me&gt;</Authors>
    <Company>sciBASIC.NET Foundation</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) sciBASIC.NET Foundation</Copyright>
    <PackageTags>scibasic;sqlite3;database;btree;sql-parser;reader;writer;managed</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>A pure managed SQLite3 database file reader and writer for sciBASIC# - the native SQLite engine is not required. Reading: Sqlite3Database.OpenFile opens a .db file, exposes the DatabaseHeader and enumerates tables through GetTables / GetTable; the sqlite_master catalog is modelled by Sqlite3MasterTable and Sqlite3SchemaRow, and Sqlite3Table.EnumerateRows streams rows which are addressable by column ordinal or name. Format layer: the Core.Objects namespace covers the B-tree page structures (BTreePage, BTreeInteriorTablePage, BTreeLeafTablePage, BTreeCellData and ColumnDataMeta) and their headers; Core.Objects.Enums holds the file format enumerations (BTreeType, FileReadVersion, FileWriteVersion, SqliteDataType and SqliteEncoding); Core.Helpers provides B-tree navigation tools and the sqlite data stream. Schema: Core.SQLSchema parses the CREATE TABLE statement of each table into a column schema (SQLParser, Schema, Token) so rows can be addressed by name. Writing: the Writer namespace (Sqlite3Writer, Sqlite3TableWriter, Sqlite3Column and Sqlite3DataRow) creates a database, defines tables, inserts, updates and deletes rows and commits; the writer keeps an in-memory model and rebuilds the file atomically on Commit, after which the produced file can be reopened by the reader. Not supported: secondary indexes, views, triggers, WITHOUT ROWID tables and custom collations.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageIcon>logo-knot.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <IncludeSymbols>True</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(Platform)'=='nuget_release|x64'">
    <PlatformTarget>x64</PlatformTarget>
    <RemoveIntegerChecks>true</RemoveIntegerChecks>
    <DebugSymbols>true</DebugSymbols>
    <DebugType>full</DebugType>
    <OutputPath>../../../.nuget/</OutputPath>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Remove="test\**" />
    <EmbeddedResource Remove="test\**" />
    <None Remove="test\**" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\..\Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core\src\Core.vbproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\DataFrame\dataframework-netcore5.vbproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\BinaryData\binarydata-netcore5.vbproj" />
    <None Include="..\..\..\vs_solutions\logo-knot.png">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="README.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
